<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salem witch trials</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1692">1692</a>–<a href="/years/1693">1693</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Salem witch trials were a series of prosecutions for witchcraft in the Province of Massachusetts Bay in 1692 and 1693, centred on Salem Village and the town of Salem. Set off by the fits of young girls, accusations spread to more than 200 people. A special court convicted many on spectral evidence, and nineteen were hanged and one pressed to death before Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-phips">William Phips</a> halted the trials.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/salem-witch-trials.jpg" alt="Salem witch trials" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph E., ca. 1837-1914, artist. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Salem_witch2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
